       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Concentration-dependent bactericidal:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " inhibit DNA gyrase and topoisomerase (bacterial DNA replication)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " disabling, possibly irreversible tendinitis/tendon rupture, peripheral neuropathy, CNS effects, myasthenia gravis exacerbation; stop at once if they occur. Also QT prolongation, aortic aneurysm/dissection, hypo/hyperglycemia (usually diabetics on insulin or oral agents), C. difficile diarrhea, photosensitivity."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Prior allergy; arrhythmia-prone states (QT prolongation, uncorrected hypokalemia/hypomagnesemia, significant bradycardia) or other QT-prolonging drugs. Avoid in myasthenia gravis, CNS disorders, and known aortic aneurysm or its risk factors (eg, Marfan). Children: AAP advises second-line use only, in a few situations with no reasonable alternative. Pregnancy: only if benefit exceeds risk and no safer alternative. Ciprofloxacin + tizanidine contraindicated."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Polyvalent cations (Al, Mg, Ca, Zn, iron) cut oral absorption: give levofloxacin at least two hours before or after antacids, sucralfate, iron, zinc multivitamins. Ciprofloxacin raises theophylline levels (serious and fatal reactions reported)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
